# GOLDEN RCleaned ROverlapReq DISJOINT
# GROUND-TRUTH: the cleaning idiom. reject dR<0.4 fires exactly when select dR<0.4 passes
#   (min pairwise dR), so the two regions are complementary on that predicate -> TRULY
#   DISJOINT, even over events with absent eta/phi (a soft-false dR<0.4 excludes
#   ROverlapReq and admits RCleaned - complements of ONE predicate cannot both hold).
#   In ROverlapReq: {jet eta0 phi0, ele eta0 phi0.1}=dR0.1. In RCleaned: same jet, ele eta2 (dR2).
#
#   R1, restored 2026-07-31 by the presence model (SPEC_PRESENCE_MODEL). From
#   2026-07-25 this was pinned fail-closed at POSSIBLY: the interim
#   absent-property guard hedged EVERY negation over a possibly-absent quantity,
#   because `reject q < k` HOLDS on absence while its classical encoding excludes
#   it, and two COMPLEMENTARY REJECTS in that shape fabricated a PROVEN DISJOINT.
#   The presence model says it at the leaf instead of hedging: RCleaned encodes
#   `p < 1 or dR >= 0.4`, ROverlapReq `p >= 1 and dR < 0.4`, whose conjunction is
#   UNSAT either way `p` falls - while two complementary rejects keep the shared
#   `p < 1` model and stay POSSIBLY, which is correct.

object jets
  take Jet
  select pt > 30

object eles
  take Ele
  select pt > 20

region RCleaned
  select size(jets) >= 1
  select size(eles) >= 1
  reject dR(jets, eles) < 0.4

region ROverlapReq
  select size(jets) >= 1
  select size(eles) >= 1
  select dR(jets, eles) < 0.4
